### 1 — `walk_truth` has no guard on the Market↔Deli spine, and the point that claims to cover it is on the wrong side of the building
**Where:** corridor x 304–330, y 102–470 (PDF pt) — ~2.5 m wide, ~36 m long, ~90 m².
**Evidence:** `/tmp/crops/r0c0.png` + `r1c0.png` (green, correct); scan `x=316 → free y 102–470`. Guard status: nearest printed word 64–140 pt away and it is `Deli`/`Bakery` — the department names *inside* the sealed block, which net 1 skips as `staff_mask`-blessed; nearest aisle badge 168–186 pt (16–18 m), so net 2's badge corroboration can never fire; it sits inside **both** the DELI disk (d=64 ≤ r=130) and the BAKERY disk (d=79 ≤ r=130), surviving only because 26 pt > the 12 pt bridge.
**Truth:** customer floor — the west wing's only north–south spine, serving the Market gondola east faces and the Deli/Bakery block west wall.
**Counterfactual (run):** sealing it yields `walkable_pct 28.1`, `components 1`, `verify []`, both coverage lists empty — **every mechanical net green**, and the pre-audit `walk_truth` does not fail. That is the store-24 signature exactly.
**Compounding:** `[475, 200, "Deli customer frontage on the Market corridor"]` sits 159 pt away on the *east* side of the Deli block, in the aisle-1 corridor. The coordinate is fine for Deli frontage; the description names a corridor it isn't in, so the file reads as covering this spine when it doesn't.
**Fix type:** `walk_truth` points — added `[316,165]`, `[316,300]`, `[316,440]`; corrected the `[475,200]` description to name the aisle-1 corridor and the east-facing cooler run (body x 453–464, arcs to x=473).

